# How to cite this repository. GitHub reads this file and shows a
# "Cite this repository" button; the version is updated at each release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "From notebook to bedside: best practices in software engineering for robust and maintainable medical AI"
abstract: >-
  Companion repository of a TEF-Health training capsule. The Hello World Deep
  Learning in Medical Imaging tutorial of Lakhani et al. (2018) is taken from a
  Jupyter notebook to maintainable code in six steps: version control,
  reproducible environment, architecture, tests, documentation and automation,
  with one Git tag per step.
authors:
